    <main>
        <h1>about me</h1>

        <div>
            <img id="selfie" src="images/selfie.png" alt="A photo of myself">
        
            <!--Short intro of who i am--> 
            <p class="introduction">Hi! I'm John, a Computer Science student at UC San Diego
        specializing in Bioinformatics. I'm interested in using
        programming and computational methods to better understand
        biological problems. Outside of school and research, I enjoy
        playing tennis, spending time with my dog June, and learning
        new things.</p>
        </div>
        
        <section>
            <h2>background</h2>
            <p>I'm currently an undergraduate researcher at the Li Lab
        at UC San Diego's Moores Cancer Center, where I work with
        single-cell sequencing data to study gene expression and
        cellular development. Through my research, I've gained
        experience working with R, Python, and various bioinformatics
        tools. I'm still learning a lot, but that's also what I enjoy
        about research. There's always something new to figure out.
            </p>

            <p>After completing my undergraduate degree, I hope to pursue
        graduate studies in bioinformatics to strengthen my
        computational and statistical skills. My goal is to eventually
        work in bioinformatics or computational biology.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>interests</h2>
            <p>
                Outside of academics, I spend a lot of my free time playing
                tennis. It's one of my favorite ways to stay active and take
                a break from staring at my computer. I also enjoy spending
                time with my dog June, who has <b>his</b> own page on this website!
            </p>

            <p>
                I also enjoy exploring different topics, whether it's
                learning more about biology, improving my programming skills,
                or just going down a random rabbit hole about something
                interesting.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
